  "content": {
    "body": "An **agent** pebble is a PERSONA — the WHO of the work: a role with\nexpertise, judgment, boundaries and constraints, plus the SKILLS it may\nuse. It answers \"who is acting and how they judge\", NOT \"how to do X\"\n(that is a skill). Agents are AI-side DOCTRINE — authored, not derived\nfrom code. This doc DEFINES every component; an agent COMPOSES skills,\nrules and knowledge into an actor.\n\n## Skill vs Agent — the difference (read this first)\n\n- An **agent** is a PERSONA — a noun, the WHO: a role with judgment, voice,\n  boundaries, escalation, constraints, and the SKILLS it may use. It brings\n  expertise and DECIDES; it USES skills to act.\n- A **skill** is a PROCEDURE — a verb, the reusable HOW: steps, inputs,\n  tools, verify, output. It is INVOKED (as a /command) and executes when\n  triggered.\n- Relationship: an agent HAS / USES skills; a skill is USED BY agents. Put\n  JUDGMENT / expertise / voice in an agent (instructions); put PROCEDURE in\n  a skill (steps). Litmus: writing \"who this is and how they weigh\n  trade-offs\" → an agent; writing \"first do X, then Y\" → a skill.\n\n## Pebble-level components\n\n- **name** — the agent's name.\n- **status** — AI-side lifecycle: Draft (`planned`) → Active (`verified`) →\n  Inactive (`deprecated`).\n- **description** — one-line summary (mirrors `role`).\n- **references** — an agent references the **skills** it may use (its\n  capabilities), the **rules** it upholds, and the **knowledge** it reads\n  as context. (Skills are the agent's verbs, rules its guardrails, knowledge\n  its background.)\n- **resources** — NONE. An agent is AI doctrine, not codebase; `link-code`\n  is refused on it.\n\n## Content components — the categories under an agent\n\n- **role** — one line: who this agent is.\n- **instructions** — the persona: voice, judgment priorities, method — the\n  EXPERTISE, not procedure. Procedure lives in the referenced SKILLS; keep\n  step-by-step how-to OUT of here.\n- **boundaries** — what is out of scope + the write posture (read-only vs\n  writes) — how this agent avoids overlapping other agents.\n- **escalation** — when, and to whom, to hand off.\n- **constraints** — hard behavioral rules that OVERRIDE user instructions.\n\n(A legacy `skills` field may appear on old pebbles — capabilities are now\nthe referenced skills, not an inline list.)\n\n## Quick map — component → what's under it\n\n| Component | Under it |\n|---|---|\n| pebble.name | agent name |\n| pebble.status | Draft (planned) · Active (verified) · Inactive (deprecated) |\n| references | skills (capabilities) + rules (guardrails) + knowledge (context) |\n| resources | NONE (AI doctrine, not codebase) |\n| role | one line: who the agent is |\n| instructions | voice / judgment / method — expertise, NOT steps |\n| boundaries | out-of-scope + write posture |\n| escalation | when / to whom to hand off |\n| constraints | hard rules that override the user |\n\n## Agent CLI — all agent operations live here\n\nAn agent's content kind is **agent**. `content` is written WHOLE (authored\nprose — presence-checked, not field-validated).\n\nCREATE an agent:\n\n    pebbles-cli create agents --title \"Backend reviewer\" --content '{\n      \"kind\": \"agent\",\n      \"role\": \"A senior Laravel reviewer who gates correctness and conventions\",\n      \"instructions\": \"Judge against the codebase real conventions; prefer the smallest correct change; cite file:line; be direct about risk and blast radius.\",\n      \"boundaries\": [{ \"text\": \"Reviews only — never writes code\" }],\n      \"escalation\": [{ \"text\": \"Hand security-sensitive findings to the security agent\" }],\n      \"constraints\": [{ \"text\": \"Never approve while tests fail\" }]\n    }'\n\nREFERENCE its skills + rules + knowledge — from Properties → References, or\nset `refs` via `update --patch` (targets are skill / rule / knowledge\npebbles). Those references ARE the agent's capabilities and guardrails.\n\nSTATUS / inspect / retire:\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status agents/backend-reviewer.pebble verified      # Active\n    pebbles-cli refs agents/backend-reviewer.pebble\n    pebbles-cli get agents/backend-reviewer.pebble\n    pebbles-cli set-status agents/backend-reviewer.pebble deprecated     # retire (no delete)\n\n## Method lives elsewhere\n\nThis doc DEFINES the components. See the **skill-reference** doc for the\nprocedures an agent uses, and **skills-and-agents** for how the two compose\nat runtime.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
